        "abstract": "Modal filters (MFs) have been known for their effectiveness in protecting against ultra-wideband (UWB) interference. The most common types of MFs are formed by modifying microstrip lines (MSLs) and coplanar waveguides (CWs). The first paper, “Signal Integrity Analysis of Modal Filters Formed by Modification of Microstrip Lines and Coplanar Wave-guides”, evaluates the impact of three types of MFs on signal integrity (SI). The comprehensive SI analyses have shown that, with careful design, these MFs can be employed in signal circuits with data rates as high as 2.5 Gbit/s.",
