        "abstract": "Writing now in the Spring of 2024, the EMC Society continues to punch above its weight class in standards activity. Let me first pass along my thanks to all those who gave us feedback on IEEE 299 and 299.1 — the good, the bad, and the ugly. Those are two of the most-used standards sponsored by the EMC Society: “IEEE Standard Method for Measuring the Effectiveness of Electromagnetic Shielding Enclosures” (299) and “IEEE Standard Method for Measuring the Shielding Effectiveness of Enclosures and Boxes Having all Dimensions between 0.1 m and 2 m” (299.1). We have reviewed the feedback received, which included many substantial and well-thought-out comments and critiques. We are in the process of forming a working group (WG) that can draft a PAR (project authorization request). We have learned that the bureaucratic process to renew a standard is just as onerous as that to draft a new standard, and the IEEE Standards Association will not be changing that process. (This is different than, say, the SAE, where a simple vote of a committee can reaffirm a standard if no substantial changes are needed.) So, we will be moving ahead with those two standards and will keep everyone informed about opportunities to participate.",
