        "abstract": "This Quarter's Book Review is written by Ji Chen and is a review of the newly released third edition of Prof. Balanis' book, “Balanis' Advanced Engineering Electromagnetics.” Prof. Chen's passion for this book shows through clearly as he has used it continuously since being introduced to an earlier edition in graduate school. Younger EMC engineers should take note of this and will find that the benefits of having the book will accrue over time. In a little bit of history, I wrote a review of the first edition of the book for the IEEE Antennas and Propagation Society Magazine in 1989. The fact that Prof. Balanis has now completed a third edition of the book is indicative of this book's “staying power.” It was a very useful book in 1989 and by now has become recognized as a classic in the field. Anyone who spends a lot of time with electromagnetic theory will benefit from having a copy on the shelf and may find that (after time) it has become well used.",
